The OK path of this fixture needs the interpreter's catch-unwind to carry an
aggregate payload, which it does not: `(ok-val r)` yields the struct handle, so
`.name` prints a pointer.  Same defect as
tests/fixtures/catch-unwind-aggregate-thunk -- filed as
docs/reported/turi-catch-unwind-aggregate-payload.md.  The ERR path (the point
of this fixture) does work under turi since schema-decode-abort became a
catchable panic there too; drop this marker when the payload defect is fixed.
